WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.743
Data often comes in pieces.

2
00:00:02.743 --> 00:00:07.016
In this lesson, you will learn to put the pieces together:

3
00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:12.067
side by side with bind columns, or one under another with bind rows.

4
00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:17.117
You will also see what NA means when the pieces don't match perfectly.

5
00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.060
Let's build a bigger picture.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.564
We have three tables now.

7
00:00:23.564 --> 00:00:25.616
Demographic, with five columns.

8
00:00:25.616 --> 00:00:28.693
Initial Information, also with five columns.

9
00:00:28.693 --> 00:00:32.283
And Main Question, with three survey questions:

10
00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:35.360
urea, kilograms received, and seed quality.

11
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.567
Let's look at demographic first.

12
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:45.460
One hundred thirty five rows, five columns.

13
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.205
I write a note:

14
00:00:58.205 --> 00:00:59.909
combining data frames, column-wise.

15
00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:02.040
That means side by side.

16
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:26.073
Demographic, arrow, bind underscore cols, and inside, demographic and Main Question.

17
00:01:26.073 --> 00:01:29.620
The tooltip helps us with the arguments.

18
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.323
Run it.

19
00:01:33.323 --> 00:01:35.382
Demographic now has eight variables.

20
00:01:35.382 --> 00:01:40.733
Open it, and you see the three question columns added on the right.

21
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.380
Same rows, more columns.

22
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:06.506
Bind columns only works well when both tables have the same rows, in the same order.

23
00:02:06.506 --> 00:02:10.260
Here, both come from the same dataset, so they match.

24
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.697
Now row-wise.

25
00:02:13.697 --> 00:02:19.680
Demographic, arrow, bind underscore rows, with demographic and Initial Information.

26
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.217
Run it.

27
00:02:26.217 --> 00:02:28.728
Now we have two hundred seventy rows.

28
00:02:28.728 --> 00:02:30.880
The second table was stacked underneath.

29
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.762
Scroll down, and look at the question columns.

30
00:02:48.762 --> 00:02:51.616
In the lower rows, they say NA.

31
00:02:51.616 --> 00:02:53.247
NA means not available.

32
00:02:53.247 --> 00:02:58.140
Initial Information did not have those columns, so R leaves them empty.

33
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.791
Bind columns adds columns, bind rows adds rows.

34
00:03:18.791 --> 00:03:21.671
And when you see NA, ask yourself:

35
00:03:21.671 --> 00:03:27.020
is something missing, or did the tables just not match? Very well done!

